  "captured_utc": "2026-10-04",
  "task": "9350 (pen parity wave, capture slice K-A)",
  "harness": "live GUI editor on an isolated display; every case = fresh boot + new empty foreground mesh; perspective cases add a 64x32 sphere r=1 at (0,1,0) in the background layer; clicks are real pointer input, the stroke is ended by the drop-tool key, geometry is read back from the mesh after the drop",
  "notes": "Positions are mesh READBACK, never the requested pixels. Top orthographic rig: clicks land on the plane y = 1.0 (camera focus); 440 px per metre. Face rings are vertex indices; vertices are numbered in click order."
 },
 "law": {
  "facing_decision": "The tool's flip flag is computed ONCE, at the click that adds the third point, from the triangle (p0, p1, p2): flip = 1 when that triangle, wound in click order, faces away from the viewer, where 'away' is measured against the view direction FROM THE EYE TO p2 (perspective: the per-point eye ray, not the camera forward axis). It is not recomputed when a 4th+ point is added, when a point is dragged, when a position is typed, or when the last point is undone; a user write to the flag sticks. A collinear prefix leaves the flag at 0.",
  "ring_n3": "[0,1,2]; with flip: [0,2,1] (reversal keeps the first vertex)",
  "ring_n4plus": "Let N(i) = normalize(cross(v[i+1]-v[i], v[i-1]-v[i])). If dot(N(0),N(1)) >= 0: the list is rotated left by one ([1,2,...,n-1,0]); then, while the first corner of the rotated list is degenerate (zero normal), it is rotated right by one; then reversed-keeping-first iff flip. If dot(N(0),N(1)) < 0: the reverse decision is INVERTED (reverse iff NOT flip); for n = 4 the list is not rotated; for n >= 5 it is rotated to start at the first k in [2, n-3] with dot(N(0),N(k)) > 0 (unrotated if none).",
  "consequences": "the stored polygon need not face the camera: A2-dart, A4a-retime, A4c-typed, A4b-override all end facing AWAY"
 },
 "tolerance": 1e-05,
 "rejected_candidates": {
  "R-rot2 ring[i]=f[(n-3-i) mod n]": "fits n=3,4 only; n=5 gave [1,0,4,3,2], n=6 [1,0,5,4,3,2]",
  "R-keep0": "n=4 gave [1,0,3,2]",
  "R-rev": "every n",
  "unflipped ring [0..n-1] for n>=4": "convex n=4,5 counter-clockwise gave [1,2,3,0] / [1,2,3,4,0]",
  "T-add-live (facing re-checked at every add)": "A4e: flag stays 1 after point 4; A4e-mirror ring [0,3,2,1] (T-add-live predicted [1,0,3,2])",
  "T-live (drag)": "A4a ring [0,2,1]",
  "T-live-typed": "A4c ring [0,1,2]",
  "N-newell": "A2-dart ring [0,1,2,3]",
  "F-forward": "A3c ring [0,1,2], A3c-rev ring [0,2,1]",
  "U-recomputed": "A4b ring [1,2,3,0] unflipped"
 },
